Key product: Formation documents, EIN, bylaws, initial board resolutions, and official records file.

6. Seek Tax-Exempt Recognition, If Appropriate
Many charitable nonprofits seek recognition under Internal Revenue Code section 501(c)(3). The organization must select the appropriate structure and prepare an application that accurately describes its governance, activities, finances, compensation, and intended use of funds.

High-level preparation includes:

Confirm the intended tax-exempt organization type.

Prepare a narrative describing planned activities.

Develop realistic financial projections.

Identify expected sources of revenue.

Document board and officer relationships.

Identify potential conflicts of interest.

Prepare and submit the appropriate IRS application.

Retain all application materials and determination letters.

The Internal Revenue Service provides Form 1023 and, for some eligible smaller organizations, Form 1023-EZ. 
